# AUTOMATED PARAMETER COLLECTION

define an automated process to collect parameters from scientific and/or grey literature to populate vegetation species in Landscape-DNDC. Here is the process: iterate through each line of the file 'Site_params_GEMINI.csv'. each row represents a given parameter for a given plant species. The plant species is defined according to common_name, scientific_name, and genus. . First search the literature based on the common_name and find studies which report the parameter defined in column 'description' with units defined in words under 'units in words' and in units as 'units'. From the reviewed studies, report the minimum, maximum values in columns 'minimum' and 'maximum' respectively. If any specific point values are reported, specify these in point_estimate. Then under 'references' give the references for which you found the data. At the end of the data collection process, display the full citations for the references you cited. In the initial search, use the common and scientific names as search criteria. If you cannot find data for this, then use the genus instead. if you cannot find data for the genus, use the 'descriptor' column as a general description of the vegetative species being searched. 

implement the following modifications to procedure: be sure to always populate specifically the columns pertaining to each desired output. that is, the minimum observed value for the parameter in the literature should appear under column 'minimum'. The maximum observed literature value should appear in column 'maximum'. The point estimate should appear in column 'point_estimate'. The references for these three populated values, minimum, maximum, and point_estimate should then be populated individually in the columns 'reference_minimum' for the minimum value, 'reference_maximum' for the maximum value, and 'reference_point_estimate' for the point estimate value

update to procedure: when a given row is missing a common name, skip to the scientific name. 



